<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Classifying a function as Even, Odd, or Neither</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the function</p>
<p>\[ k(x) = \dfrac{ {@numer@} }{ {@denom@} }. \]</p>
[[jsxgraph width="420px" height="300px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-4, 8, 4, -8],
    axis: true,
    showCopyright: false,
    showNavigation: false
});
var f = board.jc.snippet('{#expr#}', true, 'x', true);
board.create('functiongraph', [f, -4, 4], {strokeColor: '#1565c0', strokeWidth: 2});
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p><strong>(a)</strong> Find and fully simplify \(k(-x)\).</p>
<div>\( k(-x) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Hence classify \(k(x)\) as Even, Odd, or Neither.</p>
<div>\( k(x) \) is [[input:ans2]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Substituting \(-x\) for every occurrence of \(x\):</p>
\[ k(-x) = \dfrac{ {@numer@} }{ {@denom@} }\Big|_{x \to -x} = {@fnegx@}. \]
<p>Remember: a term with an <strong>even</strong> power of \(x\) (including a constant, which is \(x^0\)) is unchanged when \(x\to -x\), because \((-x)^{\text{even}}=x^{\text{even}}\). A term with an <strong>odd</strong> power of \(x\) changes sign, because \((-x)^{\text{odd}}=-x^{\text{odd}}\).</p>
<p>Comparing \(k(-x)\) to \(k(x)\):</p>
<ul>
<li>If \(k(-x)=k(x)\), the function is <strong>Even</strong>.</li>
<li>If \(k(-x)=-k(x)\), the function is <strong>Odd</strong>.</li>
<li>Otherwise, it is <strong>Neither</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<p>In this case, \(k(x)\) is <strong>{@classlabel@}</strong>.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
