    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>k(x) = ({@numer@})/({@denom@}) is {@classlabel@}</p>]]></text>
    </questionnote>
    <questiondescription format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p id="description">Grade 11 Functions, Section 16.6 (Even and Odd Functions). The scenario (Even/Odd/Neither) and the model answer for k(-x) are both derived automatically by the CAS from the same general expression, so the question is self-verifying for every random variant. Tests the common misconceptions that (i) students forget to substitute -x at all, (ii) students flip the sign of every term including even powers, and (iii) students wrongly flip the sign of the constant term.</p>]]></text>
